<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cayuga people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cayuga Nation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cayuga are an Iroquoian people, one of the five original nations of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> lay around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayuga-lake">Cayuga Lake</a> in the Finger Lakes region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. They held ten of the fifty chiefly titles in the confederacy's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a>. Most sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a> and lost their lands, and today they live at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-nations-of-the-grand-river">Six Nations of the Grand River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cayuga-people.jpg" alt="Cayuga people" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cayuga_Leaders_-_Iroquois_Past_and_Present.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
